#: kcmnewsticker.cpp:60
msgid "News query interval:"
msgstr "Intervalo por rigardo je novaĵoj"

#: kcmnewsticker.cpp:207
msgid ""
"<h1>News Ticker</h1> This module allows you to configure the news ticker "
"applet for KDE's panel. Here, you can configure general settings such as how "
"often KNewsTicker will check for new articles as well as managing the list "
"of news sources which KNewsTicker will query for new articles."
msgstr ""
"<h1>Novaĵprezentilo</h1> Tiu modulo permesas agordi la novaĵprezentilon "
"de la Panelo. Vi povas agordi, kiom ofte la programo rigardos je novaj mesaĝoj "
"kaj administri la liston de novaĵfontoj, kiujn Novaĵprezentilo trakribras je "
"novaĵoj."

#: kcmnewsticker.cpp:231 kcmnewsticker.cpp:294 kcmnewsticker.cpp:324
msgid "Unknown"
msgstr "Nekonata"

#: kcmnewsticker.cpp:261
msgid ""
"Do you really want to remove the news source '%1'?<br><br>Press 'Yes' to "
"remove the news source from the list, press 'No' to keep it and close this "
"dialog."
msgstr ""
"Ĉu vi vere volas forigi la novaĵfonton '%1'?<br><br>Premu 'Jes' por "
"origi la novaĵfonton el la listo, aŭ premu 'Ne' por konservi ĝin kaj fermi "
"la dialogon."

#: kcmnewsticker.cpp:276
msgid "Edit news sources"
msgstr "Redaktu novaĵfontojn"

#: kcmnewsticker.cpp:277
msgid "&Add news source"
msgstr "&Aldonu novaĵfonton"

#: kcmnewsticker.cpp:279
msgid "&Remove '%1'"
msgstr "&Forigu '%1'"

#: kcmnewsticker.cpp:281
msgid "&Remove news source"
msgstr "&Forigu novaĵfonton"

#: rc.cpp:1
msgid "KCMNewsTickerWidget"
msgstr "KCMNewsTickerWidget"

#: rc.cpp:4 rc.cpp:5 rc.cpp:79
msgid "General"
msgstr "Ĝenerale"

#: rc.cpp:6
msgid " minutes"
msgstr " minutoj"

#: rc.cpp:7
msgid "Never"
msgstr "Neniam"

#: rc.cpp:8
msgid "Interval of news queries"
msgstr "Intervalo de rigardo je novaĵoj"

#: rc.cpp:9
msgid ""
"Here you can define in what intervals KNewsTicker queries the configured "
"news sources for new headlines. This depends generally on how fast you'd "
"like to hear about news and how much load you want to put on the "
"network:<ul>\n"
"<li>A lower value (lower than <b>15 minutes</b>) enables you to get notified "
"about news very fast if you want or need to. Please note, that it increases "
"the network traffic significantly, though. Therefore, such low values "
"shouldn't be used if you query popular news sites (such as <a "
"href=http://slashdot.org>Slashdot</a> or <a "
"href=http://freshmeat.net>Freshmeat</a>) as they have generally already "
"enough work with processing the incoming queries.</li>\n"
"<li>A higher value (higher than <b>45 minutes</b>) won't make you hear about "
"news that fast. For non-timecritical applications, it should be suitable, "
"though. The positive aspect of longer intervals is that only very little "
"load is put on the network; this saves resources and nerves, for you and the "
"system administrators of the news sites you query.</li></ul>\n"
"The default value (30 minutes) should be appropriate and reasonable in most "
"cases."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:10
msgid "Use custom names for news sites"
msgstr "Uzu proprajn nomojn por novaĵejoj"

#: rc.cpp:11
msgid "Use the names defined in the list of news sources"
msgstr "Uzu la nomojn difinitajn en la listo de novaĵfontoj"

#: rc.cpp:12
msgid ""
"Check this box to make the news ticker use the names you specified in the "
"list of news sources (available on the tab labelled <i>News sources</i>) "
"instead of the ones the news sites themselves report.<br>This can be handy "
"for news sites which report a very long or useless name."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:13
msgid "Endless scrolling"
msgstr "Senfina ruliĝado"

#: rc.cpp:14
msgid ""
"Make the scroller scroll the headlines continuously (\"endless\"), instead "
"of scrolling all of the headlines and then starting all over."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:15
msgid ""
"Check this box to avoid that ugly break and the end of the scrolling (when "
"all the headlines have appeared once). If endless scrolling is enabled and "
"the last headline has been shown, KNewsTicker will attach the first headline "
"to the end of the scrolling text."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:16
msgid "Scroll the most recent headlines only"
msgstr "Rulu nur la plej novajn titolojn"

#: rc.cpp:17
msgid "Show just the most recent headline for each news site in the scroller"
msgstr "Montru nur la plej novajn titolojn de ĉiu novaĵfonto en la rulilo"

#: rc.cpp:18
msgid "Check this button to show just the most recent headline for each news site. "
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:19
msgid "Scrolling options"
msgstr "Rulopcioj"

#: rc.cpp:20
msgid "Choose font..."
msgstr "Elektu tiparon..."

#: rc.cpp:21 rc.cpp:48
msgid "Scrolltext font"
msgstr "Rulteksta tiparo"

#: rc.cpp:22
msgid ""
"Click here to choose the font which will be used for the scrolling text. "
"Please note that certain fonts are harder to read that others, especially "
"when they're used as a scrolltext, so you should probably choose a font "
"which can even easily be read if it's moving."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:23
msgid "Foreground color:"
msgstr "Tekstkoloro:"

#: rc.cpp:24 rc.cpp:26
msgid "Foreground color"
msgstr "Tekstkoloro"

#: rc.cpp:25
msgid ""
"Click the button at the right open a convenient color-selection dialog which "
"lets you choose the color which will be used for the foreground of the "
"scrolling text."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:27
msgid ""
"Click this button open a convenient color-selection dialog which lets you "
"choose the color which will be used for the foreground of the scrolling text."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:28
msgid "To the left"
msgstr "Maldekstren"

#: rc.cpp:29
msgid "To the right"
msgstr "Dekstren"

#: rc.cpp:30
msgid "Upwards"
msgstr "Supren"

#: rc.cpp:31
msgid "Downwards"
msgstr "Malsupren"

#: rc.cpp:32 rc.cpp:51
msgid "Direction of scrolling"
msgstr "Ruldirekto"

#: rc.cpp:33 rc.cpp:52
msgid ""
"These options allow you to define in what direction the text should be "
"scrolled, e.g. to the left or to the right, upwards or downwards."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:34 rc.cpp:39
msgid "Background color"
msgstr "Fonkoloro"

#: rc.cpp:35
msgid ""
"Click this button to open a convenient color-selection dialog which lets you "
"choose the color which will be used for the background of the scrolling text."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:36 rc.cpp:45
msgid "Highlighted color"
msgstr "Emfazkoloro"

#: rc.cpp:37
msgid ""
"Click this button to open a convenient color-selection dialog which lets you "
"choose the color which will be used for the color of the headlines when they "
"are highlighted (when you move the mouse over them)."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:38
msgid "Background color:"
msgstr "Fonkoloro:"

#: rc.cpp:40
msgid ""
"Click the button at the right to open a convenient color-selection dialog "
"which lets you choose the color which will be used for the background of the "
"scrolling text."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:41
msgid "Underline highlighted headline"
msgstr "Substreku emfazitajn titolojn"

#: rc.cpp:42
msgid "Underline the currently highlighted headline"
msgstr "Substreku la momente emfazitan titolon"

#: rc.cpp:43
msgid ""
"Check this box to have the currently highlighted headline (e.g. the headline "
"which is currently under the mouse cursor) underlined."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:44
msgid "Highlighted color:"
msgstr "Emfazkoloro:"

#: rc.cpp:46
msgid ""
"Click the button at the right to open a convenient color-selection dialog "
"which lets you choose the color which will be used for the color of the "
"headlines when they are highlighted (when you move the mouse over them)."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:47
msgid "Font:"
msgstr "Tiparo:"

#: rc.cpp:49
msgid ""
"Click on the button at the right labelled <i>Choose font...</i> to choose "
"the font which will be used for the scrolling text. Please note that certain "
"fonts are harder to read that others, especially when they're used as a "
"scrolltext, so you should probably choose a font which can even easily be "
"read if it's moving."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:50
msgid "Direction of scrolling:"
msgstr "Ruldirekto:"

#: rc.cpp:53
msgid "Fast"
msgstr "Rapide"

#: rc.cpp:54 rc.cpp:56 rc.cpp:59
msgid "Scrolling speed"
msgstr "Rulrapideco"

#: rc.cpp:55 rc.cpp:57 rc.cpp:60
msgid ""
"Here you can define how fast the scrolltext should be scrolling. If you have "
"rather little space on your taskbar (and therefore a rather small news "
"ticker), you should probably set this to a lower value so that you have a "
"chance to read the headlines. For wider news tickers (and better eyes), a "
"faster text is probably appropriate so that you have to wait for the next "
"headline only as little as possible.<br><br> This value defines, after which "
"period of time the text shall be scrolled a little bit further; this value "
"is antiproportional, e.g. lower values result in a faster scrolling text."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:58
msgid "Slow"
msgstr "Malrapide"

#: rc.cpp:61
msgid "News sources"
msgstr "Novaj fontoj"

#: rc.cpp:63
msgid "Move the item downwards"
msgstr "Movu la eron malsupren"

#: rc.cpp:64
msgid ""
"Press this button to move the currently selected news source one step "
"downwards."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:66
msgid "Move the item upwards"
msgstr "Movu la eron supren"

#: rc.cpp:67
msgid ""
"Press this button to move the currently selected news source one step "
"upwards."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:68
msgid "Name of site"
msgstr "Ejo-nomo"

#: rc.cpp:69
msgid "Source file"
msgstr "Fontdosiero"

#: rc.cpp:70
msgid "Max. articles"
msgstr "Maks. de artikoloj"

#: rc.cpp:71
msgid "News sources to be queried"
msgstr "Trarigardendaj novaĵfontoj"

#: rc.cpp:72
msgid ""
"This list (and the buttons at the right) let you manage the list of news "
"sites the news ticker will query for headlines. The column labelled \"Max. "
"articles\" shows how many articles will be cached for the news sites (read: "
"how many articles will be accessible through the context menu).<ul>\n"
"<li>To add a site, you can either drag the URL of the RDF or RSS file to "
"this list from Konqueror or any other application, or use the <i>Add...</i> "
"button at the right.</li>\n"
"<li>To modify a site, you can either double-click on the particular site to "
"open a dialog which lets you edit the properties of that site, or click on "
"the <i>Modify...</i>button at the right.</li>\n"
"<li>To remove a site, simply click on the <i>Remove</i> button at the "
"right.</li></ul>\n"
"Note that you can also click on this list with the right mouse button to "
"open a menu which lets you do this as well."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:74
msgid "Remove selected site"
msgstr "Forigu elektitan ejon"

#: rc.cpp:75
msgid "Click this button to remove the currently selected news site from the list."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:77
msgid "Add a new site"
msgstr "Aldonu novan ejon"

#: rc.cpp:78
msgid ""
"Click this button to add a new site to the list. Note that you can also drag "
"a RDF or RSS file to this list (i.e. from Konqueror) to add it to the list."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:80 rc.cpp:96 rc.cpp:99
msgid "Maximal number of articles cached"
msgstr "Maksimuma nombro de bufritaj artikoloj"

#: rc.cpp:81 rc.cpp:97 rc.cpp:100
msgid ""
"Here you can specify how many articles will be cached (read: be available in "
"the context menu of KNewsTicker) for each news group."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:83
msgid "Select a source file"
msgstr "Elektu fontdosieron"

#: rc.cpp:84
msgid ""
"Press this button to open a convenient file-selection dialog which lets you "
"select a source file."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:85 rc.cpp:91
msgid "The source file of the news source"
msgstr "La fontdosiero de la novaĵfonto"

#: rc.cpp:86
msgid ""
"This option lets you edit the source file which will be used for the "
"currently selected news source. There are multiple ways to specify a source "
"file:<ul> <li>Type the URL of the source file in the input field.</li> "
"<li>Press the button at the right with the folder icon to open a convenient "
"file-selection dialog to select the source file.</li> <li>Paste an URL via "
"the clipboard into the input field.</li> <li>Drag a link from Konqueror or "
"any other application onto the list</li> </ul>"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:87
msgid "Name:"
msgstr "Nomo:"

#: rc.cpp:88 rc.cpp:93
msgid "The name of the news source"
msgstr "La nomo de la novaĵfonto"

#: rc.cpp:89 rc.cpp:94
msgid ""
"Here you can see as well as edit the name of the currently selected news "
"source."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:90
msgid "Source file:"
msgstr "Fontdosiero:"

#: rc.cpp:92
msgid ""
"This option lets you edit the source file which will be used for the "
"currently selected news source. There are multiple ways to specify a source "
"file:<ul>\n"
"<li>Type the URL of the source file in the input field.</li>\n"
"<li>Press the button at the right with the folder icon to open a convenient "
"file-selection dialog to select the source file.</li>\n"
"<li>Paste an URL via the clipboard into the input field.</li>\n"
"<li>Drag a link from Konqueror or any other application onto the list</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

